<http://data.silknow.org/object/35eb66f1-eace-3757-bba1-0cf5a90c9c8d/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Cream silk wedding dress\nBritain\n1841\n\nThe cut, fabric and trimmings of this dress and its high-quality manufacture suggest that it was worn by a bride with access to the latest fashions and a skilful dressmaker. Instead of plain silk, the bride chose a fabric with a delicate floral pattern.\n\nSilk, bodice lined with silk, skirt lined with cotton\nGiven by Miss H. Bousfield\nV&A:T.17-1920 [2011]"@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/35eb66f1-eace-3757-bba1-0cf5a90c9c8d> .

